Z||000000||reddog||10-25-2001||09:48 PM||||What are the symptoms of a bad tach filter?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||beer_stud_21||10-25-2001||10:18 PM||||As far as I know the symptom is: Tach don't work.  Mine don't work either.  Funny thing with mine is when I start the car the tach jumps all the way around and stays like it was hanging straight at 6 o clock.  Then when you shut the car off it goes back around the other way.  I went to napa yesterday and asked for a tach filter for a 2.8 chevy and they said "You mean like a fuel filter??"  They told me to get it at radio shack.  What are the symptoms of your problem or did you tach just stop working?  I'll be watching this thread closely I'm sure there is someone here that knows more about it than I do.  <P>-marlin||||reg||1
Z||000002||watts||10-26-2001||02:36 AM||||A jumpy tach, or a 'dead' tach is a sure sign of a filter failure.<P>All the filter is, is a resistor and a capacitor.  The resistor drops the voltage level a bit, and the cap trims off the spurious AC pulses.<P>You can make your own, refering to : <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/tachfilter.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/tachfilter.htm</A>  for most of the details.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||10-26-2001||03:26 AM||||Cool yellow GT reddog. <BR>I had no idea what people are talking about when they mention a tach "filter". Now I do. Sounds pretty weird though. <BR>Mine still works so I won't worry about it till it doesn't. People will probably be able to help you at Radio Shack I think.<P>Hey, do you have a collapsable fold-away clutch pedal or something? <BR>That's not an Auto is it?<BR>Just kiddin'!!<P>Great interior!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
